Kimai on FenrirOS
=================

Code in /usr/share/kimai (web root: public/). Its .env is /etc/kimai/env;
var/ (cache, logs, invoices, plugins) is /var/lib/kimai. PHP runs as _php.
Run its console as _php:
  su -s /bin/sh _php -c '/usr/share/kimai/bin/console <command>'

1. Create a MariaDB database and user for Kimai:
     CREATE DATABASE kimai CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
     CREATE USER 'kimai'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY '<password>';
     GRANT ALL ON kimai.* TO 'kimai'@'localhost';
2. cp /usr/share/kimai/.env.dist /etc/kimai/env, chgrp _php it (mode 0640),
   and set DATABASE_URL (with serverVersion of your MariaDB), APP_SECRET
   (a long random string, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`), DEFAULT_URI and
   MAILER_FROM/MAILER_URL.
3. Install the database and create the first administrator:
     bin/console kimai:install -n
     bin/console kimai:user:create <name> <email> ROLE_SUPER_ADMIN
   (as _php, as above; the second asks for the password).
4. nginx: /usr/share/doc/kimai/nginx-kimai.conf (and, optionally, the
   php-fpm pool php-fpm-kimai.conf); enable php-fpm and nginx
   (dinitctl enable php-fpm nginx).
5. After an update of this package: bin/console kimai:update -n
